  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Still a few showers/isolated storms across the\nfar southwest this afternoon. \n\nDrier air over southern Canada will continue to slowly edge\nto the south and west of central PA over the next few days.\n\nStill a few showers over the far southwest until around \nsunset today, as a wind shift line acts on higher dewpoints\nnear the MD border to trigger showers.\n\nAside from some fog late tonight, expect good weather to\nprevail on Sunday.\n\nMore detail below.\n\nCooler air arrives later tonight as dewpoints and low \ntemperatures drop into the 50s areawide (and touch the upper \n40s in the northwest mountains). There could be some fog tonight\nas well, especially across the northeast part of the area.\n\n   -------------------------------------------------------\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: A dry end to the last big weekend of the \nsummer season.\n\nAfter a summer of stormy conditions, especially on the\nweekend, this Sunday will feature lots of sun and dry\nweather for the holiday weekend, as high pressure slowly\nbuilds into the area. Low chance of a shower across areas\nto our east and north on Sunday. Went with a dry fcst for our \narea. Enjoy your holiday weekend.\n\nThere could be some river valley, patchy fog Monday and even\nTuesday morning, given light winds, clear skies, and recent\nwet conditions.",
